.TH ZEX.TOML 5 "2026-06-27" "zex 5.0.0" "Zainium OS"
.SH NAME
zex.toml \- package manifest format for Zainium .zex packages
.SH DESCRIPTION
A
.I .zex
file is a
.BR tar (1)
archive compressed with
.BR zstd (1)
containing exactly two top-level entries:
.TP
.B manifest.toml
Package metadata and install instructions.
.TP
.B payload/
Directory tree of files to install.
.PP
The
.B manifest.toml
schema is described here.
.SH MANIFEST SECTIONS
.SS [package]
Required. Package identity and metadata.
.TP
.B name
.I string
(required) — Package name. Lowercase, no spaces. Used as the registry key.
.TP
.B version
.I string
(required) — Package version. Any versioning scheme accepted; the live
resolver in
.I depends.rs
parses semantic-version constraints from
.B depends
tokens (e.g.
.IR "libfoo>=2.0" )
and falls back to plain string comparison for anything it can't parse
as semver.
.TP
.B description
.I string
(required) — One-line description.
.TP
.B license
.I string
(required) — SPDX license identifier (e.g.,
.IR "MIT" ", " "GPL-2.0-only" ).
.TP
.B maintainer
.I string
(required) — Maintainer name and email (e.g.,
.IR "Ali Zain <alizain.x404@gmail.com>" ).
.TP
.B homepage
.I string
(optional) — Project URL.
.TP
.B build_type
.I string
(optional) —
.B static
or
.BR dynamic .
.TP
.B libc_target
.I string
(optional) —
.BR musl ", " relibc ,
or
.BR freestanding .
.TP
.B edition
.I string
(optional) — Active edition (e.g.,
.BR stable ", " nightly ", " lts ).
.TP
.B ed25519_sig
.I string
(optional) — Base64-encoded Ed25519 signature over the Blake3 hash of
.IR payload/ .
Required for packages uploaded to the Zainium repository.
.TP
.B blake3
.I string
(optional) — Hex-encoded Blake3 hash of the entire
.I payload/
tree.
.TP
.B depends
.I array of strings
(optional) — Runtime dependency constraints. Format:
.IR "<name>" " or " "<name> >= <version>" " or " "<name> >= <ver>, < <ver>" .
.TP
.B provides
.I array of strings
(optional) — Virtual capabilities or alternative names this package provides.
.SS [install]
Required. Maps subdirectories under
.I payload/
to absolute on-disk destinations.
.PP
Example:
.PP
.nf
    [install]
    bin   = "/overlayer/zexlib/union/bin"
    lib   = "/overlayer/zexlib/union/lib"
    share = "/overlayer/zexlib/union/share"
    etc   = "/overlayer/zexlib/union/etc"
.fi
.PP
All destination paths must begin with
.IR /overlayer/ .
.SS [remove]
Written by the installer after installation; must be present for uploaded packages.
.TP
.B files
.I array of strings
— Absolute paths of every file installed. Used verbatim by
.BR zex-remove (1).
.TP
.B symlinks
.I array of strings
— Absolute paths of created symlinks.
.TP
.B dirs
.I array of strings
— Absolute paths of created directories (removed if empty on uninstall).
.SS [depends]
.TP
.B runtime
.I array of strings
— Runtime dependencies (same format as
.IR [package].depends ).
.TP
.B build
.I array of strings
— Build-time only dependencies; not installed by
.BR zex-install (1).
.SS [editions]
Optional. Enables edition selection (analogous to Rust editions).
.TP
.B available
.I array of strings
— All editions shipped in this package.
.TP
.B default
.I string
— Default edition if the user does not specify.
.SH SERVICES CONFIGURATION
Separate from the per-package
.B manifest.toml
above,
.I /overlayer/syshub/engine/services/zex_services.toml
configures mirrors and global install behavior. Relevant fields:
.TP
.B signature_verification_mode
.I string
— One of
.BR off ", " audit ,
or
.BR strict
(default:
.BR strict ).
.B strict
rejects any package whose per-tier signature does not verify;
.B audit
logs a verification failure but still installs (for migration/debugging
only);
.B off
skips verification entirely.
.B strict
is the only mode recommended for production. Read by
.BR zex-install (1)
and
.BR zex-update (1)
before every install/upgrade.
.TP
.B integrity_mode
.I string
— One of
.BR strict " or " balanced .
.SH EXAMPLE
.PP
.nf
[package]
name        = "ripgrep"
version     = "14.1.1"
description = "Recursively search directories for a regex pattern"
license     = "MIT/Unlicense"
maintainer  = "Andrew Gallant <jamslam@gmail.com>"
homepage    = "https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep"
build_type  = "static"
libc_target = "musl"

[install]
bin   = "/overlayer/zexlib/union/bin"
share = "/overlayer/zexlib/union/share"

[remove]
files    = ["/overlayer/zexlib/union/bin/rg"]
symlinks = []
dirs     = []
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zex (1),
.BR zex-install (1),
.BR tar (1),
.BR zstd (1)
